# The build context for docker/Dockerfile is this directory: compose builds
# with `context: ..` and redeploy.sh runs `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`,
# both from /opt/accounting on the VPS. The builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so
# everything not listed here is sent to the daemon and kept in a build layer.
#
# After the CI rsync --delete, /opt/accounting holds git's files plus only what
# that rsync excludes: docker/.env*, node_modules, .next and uploads. Those are
# exactly what must stay out of the image.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a pattern here is anchored to this directory unless it
# starts with **/.

# User uploads. /opt/accounting/uploads (~850MB) is bind-mounted to
# /app/uploads at run time and served by /api/files, so the image never needs
# it. public/uploads is where files went before 2026-05-03. Keep these anchored:
# src/app/api/payroll/timekeeping/uploads/ is source code.
uploads
public/uploads

# Secrets. docker/.env holds NEXTAUTH_SECRET, the DB password and the API keys.
# Compose reads it on the host; the build never does.
docker/.env*
.env
.env*.local

# Host dependencies and build output. The builder gets node_modules from the
# deps stage's npm ci, and a host copy would overwrite it at COPY . .
**/node_modules
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
